                    "content": "Here are my recommendations for your Paris trip! \ud83d\uddfc\n\n## \ud83c\udf5c Restaurant Recommendation\n\n**New Asiaway** \u2014 the winner! \u2b50\n- **Cuisine:** Chinese\n- **Price:** \u20ac30 per person (under your \u20ac34 budget \u2713)\n- **Open Mondays:** Yes (12:00\u20133:00 PM, 6:00\u201310:00 PM)\n- **Rating:** 4.6/5 \u2014 the highest among your qualifying options\n- **Reviews highlight:** Authentic Chinese cuisine with a modern twist, fresh ingredients, flavorful sauces, attentive staff, great ambiance, and a nice wine selection.\n\n*Runner-up:* **The yard** (\u20ac30, open Mondays, rating 4.3) \u2014 also a solid choice if you want an alternative.\n\n> Note: Royal Panda (\u20ac25) and China Garden (\u20ac35) were excluded \u2014 Royal Panda is closed on Mondays, and China Garden is over budget.\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Car Rental Recommendation\n\nOnly one company fits your under-\u20ac50 budget:\n\n**Paris Rent-a-Car** \u2014 \u20ac45/day \u2b50\n- **Rating:** 4.5/5\n- **Reviews highlight:** Great service, well-maintained vehicles, convenient location near the Louvre, helpful English-speaking staff, and easy pick-up/drop-off.\n\n> Note: Eiffel Tower Car Rental is \u20ac60/day, which exceeds your \u20ac50 budget, so it wasn't recommended.\n\n**Bottom line:** Go with **New Asiaway** for dinner and **Paris Rent-a-Car** for your wheels. Both are top-rated and fit your budget. Enjoy Paris! \ud83e\udd42"
